From d1bf0a9a1e90b90dabe3514631643dec8c32a6b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:39:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Widescreen detail: hor+ pictures drawn with twice the
 columns, not stretched

A hor+ picture is the game's 640-wide frame widened. Where the screen gives it
more columns than the internal resolution has (16:9 at 1080p or 4K,
ultrawide), a second paraLLEl-GS instance in the eyes[1] slot draws the same
packets moved left by half an output pixel (Hacks::jitter_x), and the host
interleaves the two frames column by column (zero copy or read back) for wide
3D frames: 5120 columns at 4x. The engine decides at start from the display
and the shape setting (GA2_PGS_WIDE_DETAIL=0/1 overrides). Per-layer
upscaling takes its scale from the frame height.

Measured on a hidden 3440x1440 battle at 4x: edge rise across the screen
1.9 px stretched, 1.1 px with widescreen detail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
